  "title": "c© World Scientific Publishing Company ASYMPTOTICS OF THE QUANTUM INVARIANTS FOR SURGERIES ON THE FIGURE 8 KNOT JØRGEN ELLEGAARD ANDERSEN ∗† Department of Mathematical Sciences",
  "authors_raw": "University of Aarhus, Building 530, Ny Munkegade, 8000 Aarh us, Denmark",
  "abstract": "W e investigate the Reshetikhin–Turaev invariants associa ted to SU(2) for the 3– manifolds M obtained by doing any rational surgery along the ﬁgure 8 knot . In partic- ular, we express these invariants in terms of certain comple x double contour integrals. These integral formulae allow us to propose a formula for the leading asymptotics of the invariants in the limit of large quantum level. W e analyz e this expression using the saddle point method. W e construct a certain surjection f rom the set of stationary points for the relevant phase functions onto the space of con jugacy classes of nonabelian SL(2,C)–representations of the fundamental group of M and prove that the values of these phase functions at the relevant stationary points equ als the classical Chern–Simons invariants of the corresponding ﬂat SU(2)–connections. Ou r ﬁndings are in agreement with the asymptotic expansion conjecture. Moreover, we cal culate the leading asymp- totics of the colored Jones polynomial of the ﬁgure 8 knot fol lowing Kashaev [14]. This leads to a slightly ﬁner asymptotic description of the invar iant than predicted by the volume conjecture [24].",
